                  "id": "a1",
                  "kind": "text",
                  "text": "**Belt drive.** Sf Belt imposes the belt speed v_b on the 0-junction Jb, whose effort is the friction force F. The slip w = v_b - x' goes to the friction contact Fric (a nonlinear R, F = F(w)); the rest drives the block's 1-junction Jm: mass m (I), spring k (C), velocity detector Vel and position sensor Pos.",
